    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/9/89412.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 91,
    "turn_text": "You know my background. So I was raised in abject world poverty. And, you know, I dropped out of high school at 16. I got a graduate or a undergraduate degree at 44. I got accepted to law school at 50. And Sarah Jane and I have four kids. We have nine grandchildren. We're gonna have our 10th and 11th grandchildren coming up here shortly. So I'm going from literally the meanest circumstances you possibly can in the United States of America. And I'm a member of Congress right now. And that happened in a single generation. So I'm so thankful to be here right now. I can't imagine doing anything other than representing the 750,000 Wisconsin I'd say do right now. When I say I represent 750,000 Wisconsinites, half of those are Democrats. And I look at them the same way. Those are my constituents. My voting record's proven that. The meetings that I take have proven that. The letters that we write out have proven that. And I'm really just thankful to be here. It's just awesome.",
